# Minutes: 4 [derived: 09-25's six-arm sweep took 177 s with a 26 s repack; two arms at 32 threads].
kind: profile
question: how much of the host union's per-column cost c_r8 is the down projection, the part the
  q8_K activation rule would shorten?
term: c_down = the slope over m = 8 and 16 of the unionr8_down dispatch time a layer call, per
  column, bench_v41_host --time at 32 threads, arms unionr8:4x8u0.125 and unionr8:4x16u0.0625,
  V4.1 file, Threadripper PRO 5975WX
unit: us
predict: 5.0..8.5
condition: just time-cpu-v41-host --threads 32 --rounds 3 --seconds 24 --warmup 3 --arms
  unionr8:4x8u0.125,unionr8:4x16u0.0625 under the lease, both arms' outputs bit-equal to the union
  shape (the bench's pre-timing check), the witness io pressure under 1 % and no other heavy
  process; the fit is t = 160 x (a + c m) per dispatch kind, as 09-25#h3tile-ab fitted the whole
decide-in: open the q8_K down round at the measured c_down, its band re-run in the flow model at the
  id prefix (the +7.8..+10.3 % at lcg P 4096 was the list-384 row's; the prefix's union carries more
  host columns), with its sigma and e2e count pin cost named in the spec
decide-below: the down share is small: q8_K saves under 1.1 us a column; re-run the flow model at
  the measured split and rank q8_K behind (c') if its gain drops under +5 %
decide-above: down carries more than its instruction share: q8_K's gain is larger than the 22 %
  column model; re-derive Delta c from the measured split and open the round with that band
